    "done_when": "Prototype the topology read capped at second point derivatives, to measure whether removing the third and fourth derivatives the saddle curvature corrections take brings the cold compile under the 60 s clause without losing saddle accuracy. The measured facts behind this: the point jet costs 43,632, 97,639, 260,060 and 753,448 expanded equations at orders one to four, and the 132-cell read compiles cold in about 772 s with 0.83 million equations, so the fourth derivative dominates it; the hand-tangent custom rule made orders two to four heavier, not lighter (cfs-point-jet-custom-rule run r-20261008T122151393511). Build the prototype as a module under the assigned prototype directory that reuses nova.equilibrium.topology internals and replaces only the curvature-correction derivatives (around topology.py _curvature_derivatives) by finite differences of the analytic kernel Hessian evaluated at a small stencil around the null, its spacing chosen and stated, with the Hessian itself from plain autodiff. Done when the report at the assigned path holds: (1) cold compile wall, unique and expanded equations, serialized executable bytes and host RSS of the prototype read and of the current read at 132, 550 and 2,000 cells, in fresh cache-disabled processes on the H200, one job; (2) on the weak-rotation limited and diverted single-null analytic states at those rungs, the axis and X-point positions, saddle-neighbourhood membership error and the curvature values from both reads against the analytic values, with the difference between the two reads per quantity; (3) the stencil-spacing sensitivity of the curvature values over three spacings; (4) a verdict on whether the order-two read meets 60 s and keeps saddle accuracy within the design budgets. Every heavy measurement runs on the H200 through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (the targets), or as one sbatch job on --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 with an explicit --mem and --time sized to finish; one measurement is one job that loops over its rows inside the allocation and persists each row as it lands, never a job array; on the compute node uv is not invoked and the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python runs directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree and TMPDIR=/tmp exported before submission and inside the payload; configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True; cold compiles run in fresh processes with the persistent cache disabled before jax is imported. Any wait names every job in wait_condition and is declared on the job that finishes last as wait_probe [\"sacct\",\"-n\",\"-X\",\"-P\",\"-j\",\"(job id)\",\"-o\",\"State\"] and wait_terminal [\"COMPLETED\",\"FAILED\",\"CANCELLED\",\"TIMEOUT\",\"OUT_OF_MEMORY\",\"NODE_FAIL\"] as JSON lists. Prototype code lives only under the assigned scripts/prototypes directory and changes no file under nova/ or tests/; it may import nova internals. Every number in the report carries its job id and log path. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies, write the manifest before every wait, list every commit, and set status complete, blocked or failed yourself.",
